  "facts": [
    "Opened on April 27, 1985, the 7,510‑metre Vallavik Tunnel sliced through Vestland’s rugged terrain, becoming a vital artery on National Road 13 for commuters and tourists alike.",
    "In 2013, a 600‑metre branch sprouted near the tunnel’s southern end, linking it to the newly built Hardanger Bridge and passing directly over the older Djønno Tunnel.",
    "The tunnel’s construction showcased Norwegian engineering prowess, blending a lengthy 24,640‑foot passage with seamless integration into the region’s expanding road network."
